  <section class="lp-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">01 / Choose around your workload</p><h2>Which LinkedIn lead generation<br>tool fits your team?</h2><p>A solo seller needs a manageable queue. A team also needs ownership, shared visibility and a way to avoid contacting the same buyer twice.</p></div>
    <div class="sg-table-wrap"><table class="lp-table sg-table" role="table"><caption>Eight LinkedIn automation tools: suitable work, where they run and the main drawback</caption><thead><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Tool</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Good fit</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Where it runs</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">The drawback</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for p in guide.providers %}<tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader"><a href="#{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }}</a></th><td role="cell" data-label="Good fit">{{ p.fit }}</td><td role="cell" data-label="Where it runs">{{ p.runtime }}</td><td role="cell" data-label="The drawback">{{ p.catch }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
    <p class="sg-note"><strong>Account risk:</strong> LinkedIn prohibits unauthorised tools that automate activity on its site and can restrict accounts. A vendor's safety claim does not provide LinkedIn approval. <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/a1341387/prohibited-software-and-extensions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read LinkedIn's rules ↗</a></p>
    <p class="sg-sources">Still choosing how to find prospects? Our <a href="/resources/linkedin-sales-navigator-lead-generation/">Sales Navigator vs Apollo guide</a> compares account research and access to contact details.</p>
