  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="linkedin-and-calling"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">04 / Put a conversation into the campaign</p><h2>How cold calling can support<br>your LinkedIn outreach.</h2><p>LinkedIn helps you learn about a buyer and start a professional conversation. Generic pitches are easy to ignore. A live call gives you a direct exchange: ask a question, hear the answer and agree on what happens next.</p></div>
    <div class="sg-note la-call-verdict"><strong>CallTeam's view:</strong> make calling a core part of B2B outreach when you have suitable prospects and usable numbers. Use the buyer’s role and business situation to prepare a relevant opening.</div>
    <ol class="la-call-steps">
      <li><h3>Choose the accounts worth a call.</h3><p>Check the company, current role and business reason to approach them. A connection acceptance alone tells you little about buying intent. Prioritise a relevant reply, a clear business fit or a reason to speak now.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Find a usable number and prepare the opening.</h3><p>Match the phone record to the person and company. Our <a href="/resources/b2b-lead-providers/">lead database comparison</a> covers data sources; the <a href="/resources/how-to-buy-cold-calling-leads/">mobile vs company number guide</a> helps you choose the route.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Call with context.</h3><p>If you sent a LinkedIn message, mention the subject briefly. Ask about the business issue. Let their answer guide the conversation.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Update the campaign after the conversation.</h3><p>Record the reply, owner and next action in the CRM. Pause automated messages that no longer fit. Honour a stop request across the active campaign, and keep an agreed callback with the responsible caller.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="la-call-example"><p class="lp-kicker">Example opening after a LinkedIn message</p><blockquote>“Hi [name], it's Alex with [company]. I sent you a LinkedIn note about [business issue]. We help [type of company] with [specific outcome]. How are you handling that today?”</blockquote><p>Keep the outcome specific to your offer. If the person asks for details, agree what to send and whether a follow-up call would be useful.</p></div>
    <div class="sg-two sg-after"><div><h3>Look for extra qualified conversations.</h3><p>Split comparable accounts between your current LinkedIn approach and the same approach with calls added. Keep the offer, buyer roles and review period consistent.</p><p>Compare <strong>qualified conversations and held meetings per 100 target accounts</strong>, plus the time spent. Count an account once when several channels helped reach it.</p></div><div><h3>Calls alongside email.</h3><p>Gong's cold-calling guide reports email reply rates of <strong>1.81% without calls and 3.44% with calls</strong>. Use your own campaign results to judge the effect on LinkedIn outreach.</p><p class="sg-sources"><a href="https://www.gong.io/files/gong-guide-how-to-master-cold-calls.pdf#page=2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gong's email-reply comparison, page 2 ↗</a></p></div></div>
    <div class="gr-resources"><h3>Prepare the conversation.</h3><p>Use a relevant opening, then check it before the calling session.</p>{% include "components/free-calling-resources.njk" %}</div>
  </div></section>

